#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133544 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbff5997-1801-5dec-8e3d-e3d1ff309015" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Polynomial Inequality Using a Given Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "e9adc535-4de1-5a0c-abc6-011965031379" :question/math-academy-id "e-5819" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/55018a35718d655dc2b0d67692768e7c78ee9c064f137b31435a204280734c08.png)\n\nGiven the sketch of the polynomial $y = p(x)$ shown above, find the solution to $p(x) < 0$." :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $p(x) <    0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=p(x)$ lies below the $x$-axis. These intervals are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/141519a0d0abc0d1545d940aba1fd52b15e96d81b0c10560960df2710da4937f.png)\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is\n\n$$\nx \\in (-\\infty, -3) \\cup (-3, -1) \\cup (0,2).\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** Notice that this is a strict inequality, so we do not include the roots in our solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133545 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64b71f10-5b2b-5cae-a5dc-b9c160484d82" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Polynomial Inequality"}] :question/id #uuid "b179a821-a596-54ea-91a3-4be4b2174a43" :question/math-academy-id "e-5821" :question/problem "Given the polynomial $P(x) = x^3(x+2)^2(x-2),$ find the solution of $P(x) \\geq 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $P(x) \\geq 0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x) = x^3(x+2)^2(x-2)$ are $x=0$ and $x= \\pm{2},$ where\n\n- $x=-2$ has multiplicity $2,$\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $3,$ and\n\n- $x=2$ is a simple root.\n\nAlso, $P(x)$ is a polynomial of degree $6$ with a positive leading coefficient. So, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/435846c9b0efa313b76b0e13689fb2225209d7ee1ea52e332a65bd676d97cc8f.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x) \\geq 0,$ we look for the parts of the curve that are above the $x$-axis or touching the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x \\in (-\\infty,0] \\cup [2, \\infty).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133548 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48de9cc7-5f86-51e4-a827-796f77381af2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Polynomial Inequality Containing No Constant Term"}] :question/id #uuid "0ba3ed68-03a1-5433-a8f0-c37815194c67" :question/math-academy-id "e-5829" :question/problem "Given $f(x) = x^3 - 9x,$ solve $f(x) \\gt 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $f(x) \\gt 0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y = f(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, we factor the polynomial $f(x){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{3}-9x \\\\  & =x({x}^{2}-9) \\\\  & =x(x+3)(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $f(x) = x^3 - 9x$ are $x= - 3,$ $x=0,$ and $x = 3,$ which are all simple roots.\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/91e0e81b98e7f89796c277854bec6ce0240c797fc0c3d1eda3f33ce4bc9c85a6.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $f(x) \\gt 0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is \n\n$$\nx \\in (-3,0) \\cup (3,\\infty).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48de9cc7-5f86-51e4-a827-796f77381af2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Polynomial Inequality Containing No Constant Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15cfb5b0-1833-5d4f-a6a6-ef2f79b7e99c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288455} {:answer/id #uuid "c88351da-41c4-5007-8ddc-2d03ffed92e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (0,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288456} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a3a969-ac7a-564f-bc17-17a54d317c15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288457} {:answer/id #uuid "877939eb-60b5-5803-a2f9-6b4598ea50e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-2,0)\\cup (0,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288458} {:answer/id #uuid "6320b40c-f6bb-5cbc-8620-982123e47091" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-4,0)\\cup (4,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15cfb5b0-1833-5d4f-a6a6-ef2f79b7e99c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288455} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff293843-2b74-5bf6-b93a-ccdc3beda73c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1b2fdd9-c0cd-573a-b08c-e85f6aba3027" :question/math-academy-id "q-116437" :question/problem "Given $P(x)={x}^{4}-4{x}^{2},$ solve $P(x)>0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $P(x)>0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, we factor the polynomial $P(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & ={x}^{4}-4{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}-4) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x+2)(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)={x}^{4}-4{x}^{2}$ are $x=0$ and $x=\\pm 2,$ where\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $2,$ and\n\n- $x=\\pm 2$ are simple roots.\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/8916d10a685ad90bdf11c38c0a6e12c8a641a62fd3f0dfde3de644d907b45a8d.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)>0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is \n\n$$\nx\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (2,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288460 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbff5997-1801-5dec-8e3d-e3d1ff309015" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Polynomial Inequality Using a Given Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e513284-67d4-5c57-8c1d-583e6ae3fc47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e513284-67d4-5c57-8c1d-583e6ae3fc47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288462} :answer-field/id #uuid "65a36f06-caef-5b4b-89c9-d9237deea47b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288461} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84376dfb-e756-59e2-828b-306df7eec883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84376dfb-e756-59e2-828b-306df7eec883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288464} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0fa4aab-ed2f-5c89-85e6-9a254061a0ca" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288463} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c05e5930-bd08-5b71-a631-d7a62e46265f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c05e5930-bd08-5b71-a631-d7a62e46265f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288466} :answer-field/id #uuid "82eeb5b0-dd2a-51ef-