)>0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis.\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)=(x+4)(3-x)(1-x)$ are $x=-4,\\,x=3,$ and $x=1,$ which are all simple roots.\n\nAlso, $P(x)$ is a cubic polynomial with a positive leading coefficient. So, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/691c37edf48a5d7807f7c43d73b0ac014358632a1957e3016f953af6f47c8f36.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)>0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-4,1)⋃(3,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288477 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbff5997-1801-5dec-8e3d-e3d1ff309015" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Polynomial Inequality Using a Given Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24cf249e-5442-50fd-a80c-3b0a51bf4dc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288479} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba9dddd-d5c7-5c58-b3ca-563f972e7ebe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ba9dddd-d5c7-5c58-b3ca-563f972e7ebe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288480} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5d7d6b0-7fe3-5a25-8502-f871150aea9b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288478} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d587ac8d-1a3a-5427-977f-a319c96e2cf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d587ac8d-1a3a-5427-977f-a319c96e2cf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288482} :answer-field/id #uuid "aec33351-f0cf-582f-ba67-32068ba1eed9" 