sitive leading coefficient. So, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/65a899ed4375be4681c0e4598cc4769335cabb52257a886148438f4b4f16e671.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)>0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-2,1)\\cup (2,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288530 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "48de9cc7-5f86-51e4-a827-796f77381af2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Polynomial Inequality Containing No Constant Term"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bb7a87d-90e6-5de6-a01e-e5f0679e55a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-1,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288532} {:answer/id #uuid "2d200c3a-c7b6-5490-b6f2-a7fc61ef651d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288533} {:answer/id #uuid "2fefabe4-624f-549b-aa21-8bf074067925" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [0,1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288534} {:answer/id #uuid "498dc4e1-cd80-52e3-9375-c1f2561334cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup {0}\\cup [1,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288535} {:answer/id #uuid "b348ede3-4bb7-57d1-9459-015730f7a9a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-1,0]\\cup [1,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "498dc4e1-cd80-52e3-9375-c1f2561334cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup {0}\\cup [1,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288535} :answer-field/id #uuid "d28fb417-3330-5704-a32e-b53ff423b07b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288531}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5f8f98c2-651c-5070-b539-61b041780f42" :question/math-academy-id "q-87387" :question/problem "If $P(x)={x}^{4}-{x}^{2},$ solve $P(x)\\ge 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $P(x)\\ge 0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, we factor the polynomial $P(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & ={x}^{4}-{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}({x}^{2}-1) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x+1)(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)={x}^{4}-{x}^{2}$ are $x=-1,$ $x=0$ and $x=1,$  where\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $2,$ and\n\n- $x=-1$ and $x=1$ are simple roots.\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/e6aa75d55f2776e3e2b5d029ad51ad9e39a80e49b613705a97fa01ff34113db5.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)\\ge 0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup {0}\\cup [1,\\infty ).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64b71f10-5b2b-5cae-a5dc-b9c160484d82" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Factored Polynomial Inequality"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc17c905-58e0-5c22-b3ee-09473af9a0e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288539} {:answer/id #uuid "04d6f7c1-ffd6-5ca0-8f24-6d78f4232789" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-1,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288540} {:answer/id #uuid "621cb6d1-3b73-5c7a-956a-c83ad7ee8856" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288541} {:answer/id #uuid "5ab4b90a-ca6c-5533-8ea3-fecafda52b4a" :answer/type {:db/i