b/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-3,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288546} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea7359f-a1cc-57ce-b83b-9d0997f2455e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-3,0)\\cup (0,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288547} {:answer/id #uuid "8adb1bfb-4e10-5425-aa9c-ecfa7e3c515f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-4)\\cup (3,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288548} {:answer/id #uuid "95858e22-d854-5bad-942a-d2a015ea2dfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-4,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288549} {:answer/id #uuid "9244fc97-ffa9-59d3-a471-12ce3b688c6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-4,0)\\cup (0,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288550}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ea7359f-a1cc-57ce-b83b-9d0997f2455e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-3,0)\\cup (0,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288547} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac07d98c-0ca1-51fa-89bd-e9327c978125" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93512429-4252-5f57-bd68-033768354dcc" :question/math-academy-id "q-87672" :question/problem "Given $P(x)=12{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}-{x}^{4},$ solve $P(x)>0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality $P(x)>0,$ we need to find the values of $x$ for which the curve $y=P(x)$ lies above the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, we factor the polynomial $P(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & =12{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}-{x}^{4} \\\\  & =-({x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-x-12) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+3x-12) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}(x(x-4)+3(x-4)) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}(x+3)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe roots of the polynomial $P(x)=12{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}-{x}^{4}$ are $x=-3,$ $x=0$ and $x=4,$ where\n\n- $x=0$ has multiplicity $2,$ and\n\n- $x=-3$ and $x=4$ are simple roots.\n\nSo, we can graph the curve as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007649/assets/5ebfbd4e18de00fad05c4192be2147a9b9765e00fae5b74ac608e85466c21e73.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving $P(x)>0,$ we look for the part of the curve that is above the $x$-axis.\n\nBased on the graph, the solution is \n\n$$\nx\\in (-3,0)\\cup (0,4).\n$$"}]}
